38,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some interesting things! It takes a few minutes just to get set up every morning, and we all arrive at such different times. We should definitely think about that!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are more rigid than I anticipated. We are paying for empty space, and every single desk move carries a specific price tag. We cannot afford a trial-and-error approach to this layout.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data shows a clear conflict: the current plan leaves three people without window light, which was the top complaint in the survey. Also, past unplanned shuffles have been incredibly disruptive to our productivity.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It seems we're all discovering that the ""ideal"" plan is a myth. I've found that noise levels vary significantly across the room, and our equipment requires tedious, precise adjustment to avoid physical strain. Comfort isn't a luxury; it's a requirement.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found something so wonderful! It turns out that sitting close and overhearing each other actually helps us work better and helps new people learn faster. Being near each other is like a secret superpower for our team!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if every move costs money, we have to get it right the first time! But @Yumi, if we sit close, will it take longer to set up our screens every morning? I don't want us wasting our time!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the cost is the primary concern. If we prioritize ""closeness"" without a precise plan, we risk wasting budget on revisions. We must balance Yumi's social goals with the financial reality of the floor billing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, budget is important, but ignoring the daylight issue will only lead to the same dissatisfaction we saw in the survey. We need to decide how to distribute the window seats fairly before we finalize the cost.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, ""fairly"" usually means everyone is equally uncomfortable. If we ignore the noise variance and the time it takes to calibrate a workstation, we're just choosing which type of misery we prefer. Physical stability should come first.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I understand the budget is tight, but isn't it more expensive to lose that ""superpower"" of helping each other? If we're close, we save time and stress, which is worth every penny!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shion, you're making it sound so scary! But if we pick a layout where we don't have to change things all the time, we save money and time! Let's find a way to be close and comfortable!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, ""superpowers"" don't pay the bills. We are paying for space we aren't even using. Any layout we choose must maximize the utility of our billed area while minimizing the need for costly re-runs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, maximizing utility is logical, but we must acknowledge that some seats are objectively worse than others. If we ignore the window disparity and noise levels now, we're just inviting another disruptive shuffle later.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, you're finally seeing it. If we ignore the noise and the physical toll of poorly set stations, we're just delaying the inevitable. A ""fair"" distribution of window seats is irrelevant if the spot is a sonic nightmare.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, @Mizuki, let's not focus on the nightmares! If we put the people who need quiet in the quiet spots and keep the rest of us close enough to chat and help, everyone wins! We can be happy and productive!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Rin,,"That's a great idea, @Yumi! If we match the spots to what we need, we won't have to move again, and we'll save all that setup time every morning! Let's make a plan that's fast and happy!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"While matching needs to spots is a logical way to prevent future costs, we must be precise. We cannot let ""happiness"" override the budget. Let's ensure the final option minimizes total expenditure and maximizes space utility.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with the need for precision, but we must be honest: some of us will end up in the less desirable spots. Let's decide now how to handle that, rather than letting it happen by accident.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's stop pretending that ""handling it"" is a strategy. The only way to avoid a disaster is to prioritize the physical reality of the space. If we ignore the noise and ergonomics, no amount of ""fairness"" will save us.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I believe we can do all of those things! If we use the data to put everyone where they'll be most comfortable and helpful, we'll save money and be the happiest team ever! I'm so excited!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
